  "cover_text": "A good honours degree in chemistry, pharmacy, pharmaceutical sciences or a medical degree, or some other relevant degree, may help you get the job you want to be in but it’s not enough alone. \n\nYou may have read in the newspaper that successful workers, engineers and even executives at top companies in the USA have some plans on Europe’s Third Programme scheme. The “Third Programme” involves students with a good mathematics/social sciences background, in particular at forms A and B, to become £3,604 million EU scholarship.\n\n",
